WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.600
The women's

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.168
college basketball tournament

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.204
has been around for four decades,

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.905
but the NCAA has long

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:06.473
treated it

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.341
as something of an afterthought.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.410
For instance, the team contract

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.311
for the men's tournament

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:14.781
is worth $1.1 billion a year.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.750
But the NCAA values

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.219
broadcast rights for the women.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.787
Look, at that little line

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.056
at about $6 million a year.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.124
Joining me now

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:24.924
is Hall of Fame

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.059
coach Muffet McGraw,

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:26.793
who won two

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.228
national titles at Notre

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.563
Dame during her 33 years

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.165
leading the Irish coach.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.034
Thanks for coming in. My pleasure.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.369
I think that most people

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.270
will be surprised.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.972
I know I was to find out

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.173
that that women

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.842
were not allowed to use the March Madness

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.844
branding until last year.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.580
2022 was the first time

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.648
you could call your tournament

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.182
March Madness

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:52.452
and it didn't cost the NCAA a sense.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.920
So why did it take so long?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.320
Well, that's

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.321
one of the things that you saw

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:55.955
with the debacle

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.190
you talked about a few years ago

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:57.991
when the men's and women's

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.426
tournament were held at the same place

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.394
and completely, completely different.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.662
The women's on the court

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.432
branding was not existent, really.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.900
It would say women's tournament.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.334
We weren't allowed to use March Madness

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.336
for whatever reason, I'm not sure.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:11.905
But we've never really been valued

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.039
the way we should.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.941
I showed Governor Baker

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.843
that infamous video

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.079
that was taken at the 20, 21 tournament

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.781
showing that the facilities for the men

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.184
versus the facilities for the women.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.719
Governor Baker said since then and March

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.221
Madness is one example

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.889
that there have been efforts to

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.691
to move somewhat

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.960
more to a level playing field.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.195
How big a disparity,

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.496
though, is there still

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.997
in between the men's game

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:38.932
and the women's gap?

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:39.566
Well, it's huge.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.533
And I think if you want to know

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.602
how we are valued for the NCAA,

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:43.503
the women's vice

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.904
president of basketball reports

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:45.772
to the men's vice

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.973
president of basketball.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:47.674
So that shows

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.209
you exactly how important

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:50.910
they think the women's tournament is,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.978
because we don't even report

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.047
to the president of the NCAA

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:54.814
at the end of the year.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.182
When you win a national championship,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.118
do you know how much the women make?

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.352
We get zero.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:00.386
And the men, of course,

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.087
are making millions

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:01.821
and millions of dollars.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.590
So if there's a way that they can get

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.557
some of those units

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.625
over to the women's side,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.593
I think that will be something

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:09.028
that would really help the gender equity.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.363
And you mentioned the TV.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.431
We are lumped in

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.966
with a lot of other championships.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.434
So it's not just women's basketball.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.235
We're in with,

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:16.503
you know, every other championship

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.103
that they have,

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.304
they need to take us down

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.372
and sell and market

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.374
and promote us for what we're worth.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.643
So you heard Governor Baker,

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.911
the new head of the NCAA.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:25.912
What did you think of what he had

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.080
to say on this issue?

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.449
And as he begins his new term,

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.885
what is the single biggest thing

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.386
that you would like to see him

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:36.489
do to try to deal with the disparity

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.091
between the men's and women's game?

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:38.992
I think we're excited

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.126
that we have a politician in there,

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:40.960
because I think that's what

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:41.761
we're going to need somebody

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.463
that's willing to compromise, negotiate

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:44.164
and understands

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.231
the value of what the women

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.499
can bring to the NCAA

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.800
and to the tournament.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.234
I think he's

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.302
got a lot of things on his plate

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.304
between the transfer portal, the nil

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:51.738
and in

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.506
and really just valuing women

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.641
and making our tournament

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:55.675
equal to the men.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.009
You know,

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.410
we've been talking a lot tonight

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.812
about those specific issues,

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.782
the port hall, the name, image, likeness.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.651
There's not as much money

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.819
that is spent on women players

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.820
as men's players.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.955
Whether that's right or wrong,

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.156
it just is a fact.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:10.590
Does it

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.658
have, though,

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:12.358
those rules

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.627
that have the same possibility

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.529
of changing the game

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.031
as much as it does on the men's side?

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.098
I absolutely think it does.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.800
And I think that the transfer portal

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.968
Charlie mentioned, it's called

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.336
the one time transfer.

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.604
And yet you see that there are women

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.306
who have played in two, three

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.707
and even four schools.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.042
And my concern is,

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.310
what about the education?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.711
What about that degree?

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.213
What are we teaching these kids?

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:33.813
That they come in

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.148
with one foot out the door

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.249
and they can go where they want

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.350
if it doesn't work out for them,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.219
if they don't like what they're doing.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.086
If they

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.321
transfer a second time,

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:42.722
then they have to sit out a year,

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.190
but they haven't had to sit out.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.225
And that is the issue.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.526
They've been able to transfer

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.861
numerous times without that penalty.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.663
And that's been a real problem

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:51.664
because what

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:51.831
are we

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.299
teaching them about commitment

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.000
and staying

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.735
and fighting through adversity

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.136
and all the things that sports

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.239
really teaches you about life skills?

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.840
What are we preparing them for?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.542
And how do you feel

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.444
about the whole idea that

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.779
there are two sides to this argument?

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:07.547
One is

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.882
their athletes are getting an education.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.252
The other is there.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.920
Everybody else is benefiting off them.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.520
They're being used.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.122
Where are you on the whole question?

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.457
Of players being paid?

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:17.690
Well,

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.658
I don't think anybody

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.159
is opposed to players making some money,

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.262
but I don't believe in pay for play.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.029
I don't believe that

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:23.830
you should make $1,000,000

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.031
just because you're the quarterback.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.666
If somebody jerseys sells,

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:27.467
maybe they should make

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.534
some money from that.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.036
But I think it's really ruining

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.104
college sports with where we are

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.138
because the team with the most

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.740
money is the one that's going to win.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.275
If I offer you $100,000

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.009
to play at Notre Dame

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.710
and somebody offered you 300,000,

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.945
where are you going to go?

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.413
It's not about the fear

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.381
and it's not about the degree.

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.715
It's not about the education anymore.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:43.850
It's about the money.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:44.951
Coach McGraw, thank you.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:45.985
Thanks so much for coming in and

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.086
talking with us about this.

